  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers IETF Selective Disclosure for JWTs (RFC 9901): Issuer-signed JWTs with _sd digests, _sd_alg, object and array element Disclosures, decoy digests, recursive disclosures, the tilde-separated compact serialization and the JWS JSON serialization, Key Binding JWTs with sd_hash, the Issuer, Holder and Verifier processing rules, and the security and privacy considerations. It also covers two companion IETF OAuth WG drafts as their own version families, both with a build posture: SD-JWT-based Verifiable Digital Credentials (draft-ietf-oauth-sd-jwt-vc-19: dc+sd-jwt, vct, aka_vcts, JWT VC Issuer Metadata, x5c, Type Metadata and integrity) and Token Status List (draft-ietf-oauth-status-list-21, in the RFC Editor queue: Status List Tokens, the status claim, bits, DEFLATE/ZLIB compression and Referenced Token validation). Pre-RFC SD-JWT drafts and older SD-JWT VC and Status List revisions are legacy lines with upgrade checklists. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions, issuance and disclosures, presentation and key binding, verification, SD-JWT VC and the status list.",
